{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 3c884a7d, identifiers (c+d): an unindexed target\nkeeps its 404. 410 stays the answer of a retired object that a\nrequest reached.\n\n1. In enforce mode the outer route answers 404 for a target that the\n   new index does not list. It does not reach the object. An old room\n   link gets that 404 after the cutover, the same as an ID that never\n   existed.\n2. 410 with the error word room-retired and the member reader stays\n   as ruling e46dd964 gave it. A request gets it when it reaches an\n   object whose database holds rows and no format word. Two routes\n   reach such an object: a Worker in register mode, and a creation\n   that names an old scope ID.\n3. The outer route does not answer 410 for an unindexed target. It\n   cannot tell an old room from an ID that never existed. The scope\n   ID form sc_... does not change, and the head reads no old index\n   row (ruling e7787de0).\n4. Do not seed the new index with retired rows. That adds an index\n   state and a deployment step for rooms that Hugh retired on\n   9 November.\n5. Keep the guard that refuses to set up an unknown target. That\n   guard is the reason for enforce mode.\n\nTests: one test for each answer. An old scope ID on an enforce-mode\nWorker with an empty new index gives 404 and starts no object. A\nrequest that reaches a retired object in register mode gives 410\nwith the reader commit.\n\nDocuments: the cutover section of docs/operate-a-service.md says\nboth in two sentences. An old room link answers 404 on a Worker in\nenforce mode, because the new index does not list the room. A\nrequest that reaches a retired room answers 410 and names the\nreader commit.\n\nAll seven Worker configurations set enforce today. So a person with\nan old link sees 404. The room inventory act that I file before the\ndeployment lists each retired room and its reader commit. That act\nand the docs section are where a person finds the reader.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}